# Frontend rules

## Stack
- Next.js 16 App Router.
- React 19 functional components and hooks.
- TypeScript strict.
- MobX only for durable client-side/domain UI state that genuinely benefits from observability.
- SCSS Modules for component styles.

## Rendering
- Prefer Server Components by default.
- Add `"use client"` only for interactivity/browser APIs/client stores.
- Keep client component boundaries as small as practical.
- Do not move server state into MobX. Fetch/cache server state using server components or an explicit data layer.

## Structure
Use feature-oriented organization. Example:

```text
apps/web/src/
  app/
  features/
    auth/
    chat/
    models/
    generations/
    billing/
    usage/
    projects/
  shared/
    ui/
    api/
    lib/
    styles/
```

Within a feature, use focused folders only when useful: `components/`, `stores/`, `services/`, `types/`.

## Components/styles
- One primary component per component file.
- Components use PascalCase.
- Co-locate `style.module.scss` with the component when the style is component-specific.
- Keep design tokens in shared style/token files; do not duplicate colors/spacings throughout components.
- Prefer semantic UI state (`loading`, `streaming`, `failed`) over ad-hoc booleans.

## API/security
- Browser code calls only Vimla backend endpoints.
- Never call ProxyAPI or future direct model providers from the browser.
- Never expose ProxyAPI/provider keys through `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` variables.
- Treat all server responses as typed contracts from `packages/contracts`.
- Do not calculate authoritative balance/provider cost in the browser.

## Usage UI
- Subscription percentage is derived display state only.
- Never persist `usagePercent` as authoritative client/business state.
- UI may show approximate percentage while streaming, but backend settlement is authoritative.
- Top-up UI must not imply that provider-cost rubles are user-owned withdrawable money.

## Removed legacy rules
Do not introduce Pixi.js, canvas/editor architecture, constraint layout, SceneRenderer or ElementFactory. Those belonged to another project and are not part of Vimla.
